# Local dev environment — the image builds its own venv from
# requirements.lock (see Dockerfile). `**/` prefixes are required, not
# decorative: Docker only matches a bare pattern like `__pycache__/` at the
# build context root, so without it every nested `app/**/__pycache__`
# (there are several, from local pytest runs) would still ship.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Local data the image never ships (SQLite files, local-disk vault
# fallback) — see .gitignore for the same exclusions in source control.
.data/
**/*.db*

# Test suite + test-only dependency files — requirements-dev.lock installs
# pytest/httpx/moto, which never belong in the runtime image (that's the
# whole point of the requirements.txt / requirements-dev.txt split).
tests/
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-dev.lock

# Dev/build-time tooling and fixtures, not read by the running app.
scripts/
demo/

# Secrets and VCS/editor noise.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
README.md
